  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Welcome, Scientist!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "This is a **check-in**, not a test. Scientists are curious and not afraid to guess. Show us what you know and where you are curious to learn more."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "emoji": "🧪",
      "alt": "Science time!",
      "caption": "Science time!"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 1: Solids, liquids and gases"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Matter comes in three main states. A **solid** keeps its shape. A **liquid** flows and takes the shape of its container. A **gas** spreads out to fill all the space. Heating can **melt** a solid or **boil** a liquid; cooling can **freeze** it or make a gas **condense**."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "What do we call ice turning into water?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Freezing"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Melting"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "Evaporating"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "b"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 2: The water cycle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Water **evaporates** from seas and puddles, rises as vapour, **condenses** into clouds and falls as **rain**. Rivers carry it back to the sea."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "What happens when water vapour cools in the sky?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "It condenses into clouds"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "It turns into rock"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "It disappears forever"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "a"
        ]
      }
    },
